title: InnChatter
act: Survey
location: Inn
scenario: The road
when: $act == Act.Survey
---
// What the regulars of the inn say to each other. The game plays this group on a runner of the inn's own scene, as
// captions, while the cartographer is near: it stops when the cartographer leaves the inn and the inn's scene goes.
=> Wim: That cow was in my field.
=> Saul: That cow was in my field first.
=> Wim: The steward drinks alone. Never trust a man who drinks alone.
=> Saul: The stones walked again. Hedda says it's ghosts.
=> Wim: Map maker's been in the cellar. <<if $cellar_allowed>>
===

title: InnChatter
act: Castle
location: Inn
scenario: The feast
when: $act == Act.Castle
---
=> Wim: The castle is having a feast. With our ale.
=> Saul: With our flour, too, if Bram has any.
=> Wim: The peddler's gone up to the castle. More money there.
===

title: InnChatter
act: Fair
location: Inn
scenario: The hearing
when: $act == Act.Fair or $act == Act.Mine
---
=> Wim: The hearing's at noon. I'll be at the front.
=> Saul: You'll be asleep at the back.
=> Wim: They say the map maker went down the mine. <<if $act == Act.Fair>>
=> Saul: They say Jory came up singing. <<if $jory_found>>
===

title: CampChatter
act: Mine
location: Mine
scenario: The collapse
when: $act == Act.Mine
---
// The miners at the camp fire, on the camp's own runner.
=> Miner: Jory knew the old galleries better than anyone.
=> Miner: The lantern folk. I saw them once. Green, like a cat's eyes.
=> Miner: Three measures of oil. That's one shift, if you're careful.
=> Miner: The steward came by. Went down without a word to Gudrun. <<if $corvin_in_mine>>
=> Miner: He's up! Jory's up! <<if $jory_found>>
===
